\ port/lab/jitwords.4 - on a design with the JIT gene, after port/strings.4:
\ the string words again, as its JIT takes them. It translates a word only
\ if it can translate every word the word calls, and the return stack only
\ in order down the page (an R> in each arm of an IF is refused); the
\ design's SCAN is an operation it has no stencil for, and the kernel's HERE
\ and PAD read a variable it has none for either (so <# and the rest are
\ here again). One such word left every word above it interpreted: on
\ loop.sh 32.8 million dispatches of fastest-x86-64's were the interpreter's.
\ Here they are loops the JIT compiles: shorter than the call into the
\ interpreter the C would cost.

BASE @  DECIMAL
\ An error's message on a jitexec design: through EXECUTE from here on, so
\ a word with an ABORT" is still translated. Its THROW then cannot unwind
\ native code (compile.4's depth): these are the port's and the shell's
\ fatal errors - out of memory, the locals' save stack - which end the
\ shell on a design as a fault does. interp.4's, a forth command's, before.
' (ABORT-MSG) ?EXEC-XT
: HERE ( --- c-addr )  DP @ ;
: PAD ( --- c-addr )  DP @ 160 + ;
: CSTRLEN ( c-addr --- u )  DUP BEGIN DUP C@ WHILE 1+ REPEAT SWAP - ;
: SCAN ( c-addr1 u1 c --- c-addr2 u2 )     \ relf's: exactly c
  >R BEGIN DUP WHILE OVER C@ R@ <> WHILE 1- SWAP 1+ SWAP REPEAT THEN R> DROP ;
VARIABLE CMP-D                                   \ COMPARE's u2-u1
: COMPARE ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- n )
  ROT 2DUP - CMP-D ! MIN                         ( a1 a2 min )
  BEGIN DUP PORT-CELL < 0= WHILE 2 PICK @ 2 PICK @ = WHILE
    PORT-CELL - ROT PORT-CELL + ROT PORT-CELL + ROT
  REPEAT THEN
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    2 PICK C@ 2 PICK C@ - ?DUP IF NIP NIP NIP 0< IF -1 ELSE 1 THEN EXIT THEN
    1- ROT 1+ ROT 1+ ROT
  REPEAT DROP 2DROP
  CMP-D @ DUP 0> IF DROP -1 EXIT THEN  0< IF 1 ELSE 0 THEN ;
: STR-EQ? ( c-addr1 u1 c-addr2 u2 --- f )
  ROT OVER <> IF DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN           ( a1 a2 u )
  BEGIN DUP PORT-CELL < 0= WHILE
    2 PICK @ 2 PICK @ <> IF DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
    PORT-CELL - ROT PORT-CELL + ROT PORT-CELL + ROT
  REPEAT
  BEGIN DUP WHILE
    2 PICK C@ 2 PICK C@ <> IF DROP 2DROP 0 EXIT THEN
    1- ROT 1+ ROT 1+ ROT
  REPEAT DROP 2DROP -1 ;
\ the kernel's pictured numbers, on this PAD (its <# reached the kernel's)
: HOLD ( c --- )  -1 HLD +!  HLD @ C! ;
: # ( ud1 --- ud2 )  BASE @ MU/MOD ROT DUP 9 > IF 7 + THEN 48 + HOLD ;
: #S ( ud --- 0 0 )  BEGIN # 2DUP OR 0= UNTIL ;
: SIGN ( n --- )  0< IF 45 HOLD THEN ;
: <# ( --- )  PAD HLD ! ;
: #> ( ud --- c-addr u )  2DROP HLD @ PAD OVER - ;
BASE !
